    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0548" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg501"/>

                <head>364. Telegram 1126 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d364-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-10">November 10, 1955, 3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d364-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d364-1"/>
                <p>1126. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>With reference Taipei’s 426 to Department repeated Geneva 104, assumption here
                    has been Koo has been kept generally informed principal developments my talks
                    with Wang and it should therefore come as no surprise to GRC that renunciation
                    of force declaration being discussed. GRC should also be well aware of this from
                    Secretary’s speeches and other public statements on subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
